<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sumerian King List</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sumerian King List is an ancient Mesopotamian text listing the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumer">Sumer</a> and the cities that held kingship. It mixes legendary and historical rulers. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elamite-confederation">Elamite Confederation</a> profiles refer to it as a source.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sumerian-king-list.jpg" alt="Sumerian King List" width="320" height="339" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photograph: unknown&amp;gt; Transcription: Stephen Herbert Langdon (1876-1937) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Weld-Blundell_Prism_with_transcription_by_Stephen_Herbert_Langdon_(1876-1937).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
